
==============================================================================
S1. Conjugacy T_+(-n) = -T_-(n) on odd n (master sheet criterion)
==============================================================================
odd n in [-20001, 20001]: violations of T_+(-n) = -T_-(n): 0
PROVED (one line): 3(-n)+1 = -(3n-1) and v2 is sign-blind.
Consequence: a condition proved for ALL odd integers under 3n+1 is SHEET-BLIND;
a condition whose proof uses n>0 at b=+1 (equivalently B>0 with b=+1) is SIGN-SPECIFIC.

==============================================================================
S2. The three positive 3n-1 cycles and the plus-sheet {1}: gate data
==============================================================================
b=+1 cycle [1]: word [2], K=2, L=1, B=1, Delta=2^K-3^L=1, q=|Delta|/gcd(B,|Delta|)=1, n0=bB/Delta=1, sign(b/Delta)->positive members
b=-1 cycle [1]: word [1], K=1, L=1, B=1, Delta=2^K-3^L=-1, q=|Delta|/gcd(B,|Delta|)=1, n0=bB/Delta=1, sign(b/Delta)->positive members
b=-1 cycle [5, 7]: word [1, 2], K=3, L=2, B=5, Delta=2^K-3^L=-1, q=|Delta|/gcd(B,|Delta|)=1, n0=bB/Delta=5, sign(b/Delta)->positive members
b=-1 cycle [17, 25, 37, 55, 41, 61, 91]: word [1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 4], K=11, L=7, B=2363, Delta=2^K-3^L=-139, q=|Delta|/gcd(B,|Delta|)=1, n0=bB/Delta=17, sign(b/Delta)->positive members
Sign law (signed_cycles sec.3, PROVED): every member has the sign of b/Delta, so a
POSITIVE 3n+1 cycle needs Delta>0 (K/L > log_2 3) while a POSITIVE 3n-1 cycle needs
Delta<0 (K/L < log_2 3).  The three minus cycles have Delta = -1, -1, -139 (<0);
the plus cycle {1} has Delta = +1.  The gate q=1 itself is SHEET-BLIND; which side
of log_2 3 the clock must sit on is SIGN-SPECIFIC.

