  n=24  1193652440098/753110839881  Delta sign -1  (sign by log)
PROVED (classical, Hardy-Wright Thm 154 alternation): even-index convergents lie BELOW
log_2 3 (Delta<0), odd-index convergents ABOVE (Delta>0).  Hence, wherever the clock
of a cycle is forced to be a convergent, a positive 3n+1 cycle sits on an ODD-index
convergent and a positive 3n-1 cycle on an EVEN-index one.  Sign-specific refinement.
11/7 = (p_2 + 1*p_3)/(q_2 + 1*q_3) = (3+8)/(2+5) with a_4 = 2: the unique
intermediate fraction between the convergents 3/2 and 19/12 (j=1 of a_4-1=1); NOT a convergent.
1/1 = p_0/q_0, 3/2 = p_2/q_2 (even index, Delta<0) carry the minus cycles {1}, {5,7};
2/1 = p_1/q_1 (odd index, Delta>0) carries the plus cycle {1}.
  clock 1/1: |Delta|=1, tier-A cap 3^L/(4L)=0.750 (OUT), tier-B cap 3^L/(2L)=1.500 (in)
  clock 3/2: |Delta|=1, tier-A cap 3^L/(4L)=1.125 (in), tier-B cap 3^L/(2L)=2.250 (in)
  clock 11/7: |Delta|=139, tier-A cap 3^L/(4L)=78.107 (OUT), tier-B cap 3^L/(2L)=156.214 (in)
  clock 2/1: |Delta|=1, tier-A cap 3^L/(4L)=0.750 (OUT), tier-B cap 3^L/(2L)=1.500 (in)
The seven-cycle's |Delta|=139 exceeds the tier-A cap 78.107 but not the tier-B cap 156.214:
consistent with the pillai lane (tier B = convergent or extreme intermediate; 11/7 is extreme).

==============================================================================
S4. Eliahou product identity 2^K/3^L = prod(1 + b/(3 n_i)) on the four known cycles
==============================================================================
b=+1 (1,): |Delta|/3^L = 0.3333 <= plus sheet: (1+1/(3N))^L - 1 = 0.3333  (N=min=1)
b=-1 (1,): |Delta|/3^L = 0.3333 <= minus sheet: 1-(1-1/(3N))^L = 0.3333  (N=min=1)
b=-1 (5, 7): |Delta|/3^L = 0.1111 <= minus sheet: 1-(1-1/(3N))^L = 0.1289  (N=min=5)
b=-1 (17, 25, 37, 55, 41, 61, 91): |Delta|/3^L = 0.0636 <= minus sheet: 1-(1-1/(3N))^L = 0.1294  (N=min=17)
PROVED identity, SHEET-BLIND (pillai S4 already states it for b=+-1).
Legendre tier-A thresholds N_min(L) (smallest cycle minimum that forces K/L convergent):
  L=  2: plus sheet N_min=6, minus sheet N_min=6, 4L^2/3=5.33
  L=  5: plus sheet N_min=34, minus sheet N_min=33, 4L^2/3=33.33
  L=  7: plus sheet N_min=67, minus sheet N_min=65, 4L^2/3=65.33
  L= 12: plus sheet N_min=194, minus sheet N_min=191, 4L^2/3=192.00
  L= 41: plus sheet N_min=2248, minus sheet N_min=2235, 4L^2/3=2241.33
  L= 53: plus sheet N_min=3754, minus sheet N_min=3737, 4L^2/3=3745.33
The seven-cycle has N=17 < N_min(7) on the minus sheet, so the convergent theorem does not
apply to it, and indeed 11/7 is not a convergent: the theorem's HYPOTHESIS (a large minimum)
is what the sheets do not share.  {5,7} has N=5 < N_min(2)=3? no:
  N_min(2, minus) = 6, and {5,7} with N=5 does satisfy it; 3/2 is a convergent.

==============================================================================
S5. Census: odd n <= X on the 3n-1 sheet fall into the three known cycles (basin sizes)
==============================================================================
X = 10000000: odd starts 5000000; every one reaches a known cycle (no fourth cycle, no escape).
  basin of [1]: 1636054 odd starts (0.327211)
  basin of [5, 7]: 1623149 odd starts (0.324630)
  basin of [17, 25, 37, 55, 41, 61, 91]: 1740797 odd starts (0.348159)
  longest first-drop-or-cycle-hit segment: 172 accelerated steps at n=5960769
  census time 5.6s (timing line, not a result)
FINITE-EXACT consequence: any fourth positive 3n-1 cycle has minimum element N > 10^7,
i.e. N >= 10000001 (odd).  Mirror of Barina's 2^68 (CITED, plus sheet); the minus sheet
has NO published verification comparable to 2^68, only this repo's censuses.
control: every odd n <= 1000000 reaches 1 under 3n+1 (Barina 2020 CITED: all n < 2^68).

==============================================================================
S6. Length bounds for a hypothetical cycle from Eliahou + tier A + convergent spacing
==============================================================================
Chain (PROVED given CITED inputs): a positive cycle with minimum N and L odd terms has
  |Delta|/3^L <= e^{L/(3N)} - 1 (plus) or <= L/(3N) (minus, Bernoulli);
  if that is <= 1/(4L) then |log_2 3 - K/L| < 1/(2L^2) and K/L is a convergent (Legendre);
  with K/L = p_n/q_n, L = m q_n, |K - L log_2 3| = m |q_n a - p_n| > m/(q_n + q_{n+1})
  (Hardy-Wright Thm 171 form).  Plus sheet: y <= e^y - 1 = Delta/3^L <= e^{L/(3N)} - 1 <=
  (L/(3N)) e^{L/(3N)}, so q_n (q_n+q_(n+1)) >= 3 N ln2 * e^{-L_A/(3N)}.  Minus sheet: L >= 2 and
  |Delta|/3^L = 1 - e^{-y} <= 1/(4L) <= 1/8 give y <= y0 = -ln(7/8) and 1-e^{-y} >= c0 y with
  c0 = (1-e^{-y0})/y0, so q_n (q_n+q_(n+1)) >= c0 * 3 N ln2.  (L = 1 is the trivial clock: n_0 =
  b/(2^k-3) is integral only for k = 1, 2, giving {1} at b = -1, +1; no tier needed.)
plus sheet, N = 2^68 (Barina): tier A holds for every L <= L_A = 14878203146 (sqrt(3N/4) = 1.487820e+10)
  spacing threshold factor*3*N*ln2 = 6.137428e+20 (factor = 1.000000)
  convergents on the correct side with q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) >= threshold: first is n=23, 217976794617/137528045312
  none of them has q_n <= L_A, so NO positive cycle (other than the trivial/known ones)
  has L <= 14878203146: every hypothetical cycle on this sheet has L > 14878203146.
  first three surviving clocks (K/L reduced), the minimal unresolved conjunction lives there:
    n=23: K/L = 217976794617/137528045312, cycle length L = m*137528045312, m>=1, q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) = 122487824959452069865216
    n=25: K/L = 8573543875303/5409303924479, cycle length L = m*5409303924479, m>=1, q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) = 62594943316503790956189881
    n=27: K/L = 18340740190704/11571718688839, cycle length L = m*11571718688839, m>=1, q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) = 740833097165250920862817645
minus sheet, N = 10^7+1 (S5 census): tier A holds for every L <= L_A = 2738 (sqrt(3N/4) = 2.738613e+03)
  spacing threshold factor*3*N*ln2 = 1.946585e+07 (factor = 0.936109)
  convergents on the correct side with q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) >= threshold: first is n=10, 50508/31867
  none of them has q_n <= L_A, so NO positive cycle (other than the trivial/known ones)
  has L <= 2738: every hypothetical cycle on this sheet has L > 2738.
  first three surviving clocks (K/L reduced), the minimal unresolved conjunction lives there:
    n=10: K/L = 50508/31867, cycle length L = m*31867, m>=1, q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) = 3543674134
    n=12: K/L = 176251/111202, cycle length L = m*111202, m>=1, q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) = 33553980278
    n=14: K/L = 16785921/10590737, cycle length L = m*10590737, m>=1, q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) = 226345347662107
Literature for comparison (plus sheet): Simons-de Weger 2005 (CITED, Acta Arith. 117) no m-cycles
m<=68; Hercher, J. Integer Seq. 26 (2023) art. 23.3.5 (CITED, abstract read 2026-09-22): m >= 92,
using verification up to 3*2^69 and giving at least 1.375e11 odd members in any nontrivial cycle.
The chain here, from cited inputs alone (Barina 2^68, Legendre, Hardy-Wright 171), proves that
every nontrivial positive 3n+1 cycle has L > 14878203146 odd terms (n=21's spacing 4.746e20
falls below the sharp threshold 6.137e20); Hercher's 1.375e11 is stronger and independent.
On the minus sheet the same chain gives: any FOURTH positive 3n-1 cycle has L > L_A(minus)
and, if its minimum stays > 10^7, its clock is an even-index convergent with q_n >= 15601.

