==============================================================================
S15. Pairwise contradiction search and the minimal unresolved conjunction
==============================================================================
Cycle conditions (plus sheet): C1 gate q=1 & sign law Delta>0; C2 N >= 2^68; C3 K/L odd-index
convergent for L <= L_A; C4 q_n(q_n+q_(n+1)) >= 0.75*3N ln2; C5 no 1-cycle (Steiner), no m-cycle
m <= 68 (Simons-de Weger); C6 necklace/rotation invariance of q; C7 |Delta| = 1 only at 2/1.
Witness that they are jointly satisfiable at the level of clocks: the surviving clocks listed in S6
(odd-index convergents with q_n > L_A and the spacing inequality) violate none of C1-C7 a priori;
C1's integrality q=1 on such a clock is the ONLY untested predicate.  Pairwise contradiction:
NONE FOUND.
Divergence conditions (plus sheet): D1 D_L -> -infinity, sum q_L < infinity (glued_xor);
